{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats","id":855503,"title":"It seems that Vampires and Kuei-jin get beaten by a lot of the other splats..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-29T22:37:47-07:00","id":855503,"title":"It seems that Vampires and Kuei-jin get beaten by a lot of the other splats..","content":"But how would high ranked Vampires/Kuei-jin fare against demons, Fera, Hengeyokai and etc.?<br /> <br /> By High ranked I Mean Methuselah and Bodhisattva.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:40:42-07:00","id":855505,"title":"","content":"Didn't we just have a long drawn out series of posts here about this subject by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4851\" data-vbnamecard=\"4851\">Cheesefondue</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T23:21:55-07:00","id":855514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=855505#post855505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't we just have a long drawn out series of posts here about this subject by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4851\" data-vbnamecard=\"4851\">Cheesefondue</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he was using the top tier Vampire/Kuei Jins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T23:45:39-07:00","id":855519,"title":"","content":"That's probably because they would walk all over the competition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:20:20-07:00","id":855533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=855519#post855519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably because they would walk all over the competition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly by virtue of careless math. Kiai 6, I'm looking at you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:27:41-07:00","id":855940,"title":"","content":"Give them the same xp and I'd bet on Demons winning mostly because they're reality warpers like Mages. Werecritter level 5 gifts are supposed to be godlike and gamebreaking. Just a questionnof whether or not they'd manage to hit the bastard with them. Same with Hunter Edges","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 03-30-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:33:34-07:00","id":855947,"title":"","content":"Also, i dont know about the kuei-jin, but the vampires can replenish their number pretty easily compared to the other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:46:06-07:00","id":855961,"title":"","content":"<br /> Who wins if you compare Bodhisattvas, Legendary Garou, or Methulesahs?<br /> <br /> Mages probably. Damn their little monkey eyes. <br /> <br /> In all seriousness this just turns into a spooky creature dick-measuring contest. Cheesefondue proved the splats aren't balanced a 'lowlevel' play and the higher level supernatural powers are even less balanced than that. There is a Get of Fenris gift that prevents death, in all its forms, until your opponent is dead. Your storyteller can change or amend that, but as written, that is pretty hard for most enemies to play around. Higher level disciplines barely have meaningful stats- a Malkavian elder can make an entire city go insane if they want. There are so many potent and vague high-end supernatural abilities you just end up comparing what amount to plot devices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:23:02-07:00","id":856001,"title":"","content":"Cheese Fondue's work is really cool and interesting to be sure, though I didn't personally find it useful. When I do crossovers, I change rules anyway, so I don't care that much about who wins an arena battle by RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-30-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:34:02-07:00","id":856070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=855940#post855940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give them the same xp and I'd bet on Demons winning mostly because they're reality warpers like Mages. Werecritter level 5 gifts are supposed to be godlike and gamebreaking. Just a questionnof whether or not they'd manage to hit the bastard with them. Same with Hunter Edges</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 6, actually, and level is still variable by changer. Very, very variable, sometimes; Rokea can learn a Rank Four Gift as a starting power (Teeth of the Skin, equivalent to Gift of the Porcupine), and a legendary Red Talon Gift (Shield of Gaia, which can no-sell any one manifestation of technology as a permanent enhancement) when they &quot;merely&quot; get to elder level.<br /> <br /> Besides, Reality warping is overrated. Nexus Crawlers breath and live reality warping without consequence (it costs them little to nothing to use it and they suffer no effects of Paradox or Torment), but they still die if their Essence runs out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:52:43-07:00","id":856079,"title":"","content":"I always felt the power level went Humans, Wraiths, Changelings, Vampires, Kuei-Jin, Hunters, Mummies, Werewolves, Demons, Mages, Dark Ages Fae and then the Fae of course were weak against Humans =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:56:53-07:00","id":856150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856070#post856070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides, Reality warping is overrated. Nexus Crawlers breath and live reality warping without consequence (it costs them little to nothing to use it and they suffer no effects of Paradox or Torment), but they still die if their Essence runs out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, don't know too much about Nexus Crawlers but can they predict that the fight is going to occur, auto win initiative then proceed to freeze time and launch a half dozen rockets/40mm grenades at someone? Because Demons totally can. Not even hard for them. Also no paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:23:06-07:00","id":856174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856150#post856150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, don't know too much about Nexus Crawlers but can they predict that the fight is going to occur, auto win initiative then proceed to freeze time and launch a half dozen rockets/40mm grenades at someone? Because Demons totally can. Not even hard for them. Also no paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can change all of the air in a given block of space to poison gas, change someone's bones to rotting swamp muck, erase or alter the facial features of a target, and change bits of Garou (or, with more successes, the entire room that said character is standing in) to silver, all for a Willpower roll with no expenditure of resources (6 dice against a difficulty of 7) so I'm going to say that yes, it's probably on par with that. And they basically have at least 30 health levels on top of that, possibly as many as 100, if you fight them on their home turf; their physical bodies as created the spirit Charm don't have nearly as many before being disrupted, but all that means is that you need someone else to pursue them back into the Umbra, which is an ability sorely lacking from the suite of Fallen Lores. Also, it's doing this while trying to smack you around and eviscerate you, which it can do for ten dice to hit and ten for base damage. Wyld-spirits have a similar capacity with Break Reality, and usually get more dice to roll, but the results are... much less directed.<br /> <br /> Even more heinous are Dream Maker banes. They have Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower all at 10, most spirit Charms, and an Essence rating ranging from 50 to 300. They're basically heinously evil djinni who fulfill wishes until someone makes the drastic mistake of letting them materialize, at which point, it pretty much becomes Wishmaster time, and Fallen would likely need to be spending Faith left and right just to keep up. It has the same capacity for changing reality as both Wyld-spirits and possibly also the Nexus Crawlers (it's hard to say, since there doesn't seem to be a proper entry for the Alter Reality Charm), and is in dire need of an update for at least Revised because it has a whole bunch of obsolete Charms replaced by Blast in its writeup, so it could conceivably be even worse to face them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:45:44-07:00","id":856212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give them the same xp and I'd bet on Demons winning mostly because they're reality warpers like Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they're more like powerful Thaumaturges.<br /> They have a set of static powers that do 2 or 3 things, and then Rituals. The only exception it's the Lore of the Forge 4, but that's not very fast either. Demons can't improvise magick like Mages, they have to work hard and slow to change reality like Vampires. It's just that the effects they get after that work are usually more potent and flexible than what an average Thaumaturge gets (with elder levels this may vary, as always).<br /> <br /> I also like to think in Demons as users of Dynamic Magic, but that's wishful thinking (or house ruling)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-30-2016, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:54:40-07:00","id":856283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856174#post856174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can change all of the air in a given block of space to poison gas, change someone's bones to rotting swamp muck, erase or alter the facial features of a target, and change bits of Garou (or, with more successes, the entire room that said character is standing in) to silver, all for a Willpower roll with no expenditure of resources (6 dice against a difficulty of 7) so I'm going to say that yes, it's probably on par with that. And they basically have at least 30 health levels on top of that, possibly as many as 100, if you fight them on their home turf; their physical bodies as created the spirit Charm don't have nearly as many before being disrupted, but all that means is that you need someone else to pursue them back into the Umbra, which is an ability sorely lacking from the suite of Fallen Lores. Also, it's doing this while trying to smack you around and eviscerate you, which it can do for ten dice to hit and ten for base damage. Wyld-spirits have a similar capacity with Break Reality, and usually get more dice to roll, but the results are... much less directed.<br /> <br /> Even more heinous are Dream Maker banes. They have Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower all at 10, most spirit Charms, and an Essence rating ranging from 50 to 300. They're basically heinously evil djinni who fulfill wishes until someone makes the drastic mistake of letting them materialize, at which point, it pretty much becomes Wishmaster time, and Fallen would likely need to be spending Faith left and right just to keep up. It has the same capacity for changing reality as both Wyld-spirits and possibly also the Nexus Crawlers (it's hard to say, since there doesn't seem to be a proper entry for the Alter Reality Charm), and is in dire need of an update for at least Revised because it has a whole bunch of obsolete Charms replaced by Blast in its writeup, so it could conceivably be even worse to face them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dayum. How are you supposed to fight that? (Though, I wasn't arguing Demons could beat a Nexus Crawler. Just that a Demon could kill a vamp using reality warping. Pretty sure these things could kill most anything short of an ante if your description is accurate)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856212#post856212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, they're more like powerful Thaumaturges.<br /> They have a set of static powers that do 2 or 3 things, and then Rituals. The only exception it's the Lore of the Forge 4, but that's not very fast either. Demons can't improvise magick like Mages, they have to work hard and slow to change reality like Vampires. It's just that the effects they get after that work are usually more potent and flexible than what an average Thaumaturge gets (with elder levels this may vary, as always).<br /> <br /> I also like to think in Demons as users of Dynamic Magic, but that's wishful thinking (or house ruling)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends how you look at them. To make artifacts using Lore of the Forge they have to shape whatever effect they're trying to put into the artifact before slotting it into place. Most artifacts aren't direct translations of a given Demon Lore. Just within the boundaries. Can they do dynamic magic on the fly like a Mage? Maybe, maybe not. Depends on the ST. Can they do it at all? Yes. Dynamic magic isn't really about alacrity. <br /> <br /> You could maybe argue that Enchantment from Sorcerer does similar things, but what I generally gathered from Sorc's Enchanting was that they were hunting down already mystical objects and then using them as reagents. Why they tend to have really nasty down sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T04:33:26-07:00","id":856382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats#post855503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how would high ranked Vampires/Kuei-jin fare against demons, Fera, Hengeyokai and etc.?<br /> <br /> By High ranked I Mean Methuselah and Bodhisattva.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would go however the storyteller wants it to go. From a narrative standpoint, it seems that the undead ultra elders are more powerful than any non-mages (and the week of nightmares implies Antediluvians beat Bodhisattva, but the fight was close enough that Bodhisattva probably beat Methuselahs).<br /> <br /> At a more medium power level, I ran this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/799293-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-changers-and-suckers?p=812584#post812584\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/799293-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-changers-and-suckers?p=812584#post812584\"> Deadliest supernatural warrior: changers and suckers - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/799293-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-changers-and-suckers?p=812584#post812584\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/799293-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-changers-and-suckers?p=812584#post812584 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Continued from http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...h-the-humanity (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T12:03:57-07:00","id":856640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856283#post856283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dayum. How are you supposed to fight that? (Though, I wasn't arguing Demons could beat a Nexus Crawler. Just that a Demon could kill a vamp using reality warping. Pretty sure these things could kill most anything short of an ante if your description is accurate)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fighting a Nexus Crawler is usually not something most Garou expect to survive. The big ones are capable of killing entire packs of experienced Garou... your best bet is to overwhelm it with sheer numbers because it can only warp/splatter a couple enemies in a given turn... unless you have big guns of your own, like you happen to be an Elder Uktena or Get of Fenris and can transform into a spirit-avatar of your totem. Even that is massive sacrifice, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856382#post856382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would go however the storyteller wants it to go. From a narrative standpoint, it seems that the undead ultra elders are more powerful than any non-mages (and the week of nightmares implies Antediluvians beat Bodhisattva, but the fight was close enough that Bodhisattva probably beat Methuselahs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I thought with the Week of Nightmares it was heavily implied the Bodhisattvas would have eventually won but the Technocracy got antsy, decided things were taking too long and pressed the big red button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-31-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:42:39-07:00","id":856696,"title":"","content":"I didn't see any evidence of that. All we have on their relative tactical abilities aside from a 3-to-1 stalemate that lasted for days was that the antediluvian could survive being nuked, and the bodhisattvas couldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:24:56-07:00","id":856762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856696#post856696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't see any evidence of that. All we have on their relative tactical abilities aside from a 3-to-1 stalemate that lasted for days was that the antediluvian could survive being nuked, and the bodhisattvas couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bodhisattavas were the equivalent of Generation 4-5, rather then Generation 3, though.<br /> The whole thing is an exercise in absurd excess, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:31:19-07:00","id":856792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856640#post856640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fighting a Nexus Crawler is usually not something most Garou expect to survive. The big ones are capable of killing entire packs of experienced Garou... your best bet is to overwhelm it with sheer numbers because it can only warp/splatter a couple enemies in a given turn... unless you have big guns of your own, like you happen to be an Elder Uktena or Get of Fenris and can transform into a spirit-avatar of your totem. Even that is massive sacrifice, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bigger sacrifice for arguably less mechanical effect on the part of the Uktena, since the Lesser Uktena stats are kind of weaksauce and they lose more than just a limb. Though, to get technical, the Fenrir aren't transforming, but summoning a war-avatar with beyond-boss spirit stats.<br /> <br /> Now the Rokea and Nagah, they get off light. Leviathan and Hydra Warrior are beyond what the Uktena and Get have, with no real downsides other than that Nagah nests don't form the Hydra Warrior for just about any fight but the seriously dangerous and taxing. On the Garou end of &quot;what do you mean you had to give up something important for this?&quot; the Fianna get to be the assholes with Gift of the Spriggan layered over Warp Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:43:24-07:00","id":856828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=855947#post855947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, i dont know about the kuei-jin, but the vampires can replenish their number pretty easily compared to the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can't replace Theo Bell with Random Brujah Neonate no matter what Shovel head tactics say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:23:46-07:00","id":856958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856762#post856762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bodhisattavas were the equivalent of Generation 4-5, rather then Generation 3, though.<br /> The whole thing is an exercise in absurd excess, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Bodhisattvas fighting an Antediluvian in a supernatural storm, with all sorts of were-creatures in the mix, with spirit nukes, and a giant sun reflecting satellite... I thought for a minute I had picked up one of my Rifts books instead of V:tM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T04:06:19-07:00","id":857050,"title":"","content":"I usually had every one start with 100 freebie points, max 20 in backgrounds. Garou could buy rank up to 3rd at 20pts per rank. Every seemed to be very even then. As for the nexus crawler, even large ones seemed to fall easily to rank 4 or greater packs. Paws of the new born cub plus double damage, extra rage, spirit control and fetishes tended to put payed to any spirit below minor incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:45:18-07:00","id":857153,"title":"","content":"I seem to be totally off-base regarding the Week of Nightmares... huffing glue is worse than I thought. Oops.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856792#post856792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bigger sacrifice for arguably less mechanical effect on the part of the Uktena, since the Lesser Uktena stats are kind of weaksauce and they lose more than just a limb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw stats for Lesser Uktena in the tribebook or Axis Mundi. Maybe you are referencing the lackluster stats in that one Mind's Eye book? I don't like going to other systems for statistics and see those as apocryphal guidelines at best. I figured it was implied to be a 'win button' power that then requires your character to slither off into Uktena's tribal homeland after you get your crowning moment of awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=857050#post857050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually had every one start with 100 freebie points, max 20 in backgrounds. Garou could buy rank up to 3rd at 20pts per rank. Every seemed to be very even then. As for the nexus crawler, even large ones seemed to fall easily to rank 4 or greater packs. Paws of the new born cub plus double damage, extra rage, spirit control and fetishes tended to put payed to any spirit below minor incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, if you give Paws to Garou who are not rank 5, I imagine it will be easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-01-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T10:50:23-07:00","id":857188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=856640#post856640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... I thought with the Week of Nightmares it was heavily implied the Bodhisattvas would have eventually won but the Technocracy got antsy, decided things were taking too long and pressed the big red button.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's mention in the...Nagah breedbook? And another place, I think one of the supplements for &quot;of-the-East&quot; that says, essentially, that the omens read that <i>eventually </i>the bodhisattvas would have pulled out the win - two of them would die, but Black Earth Boy would survive. That may be what you're thinking of.<br /> <br /> The Union wasn't really aware of how the fight was going and wouldn't have listened to somebody's psychic premonitions, so in absence of a clear picture of the scenario the nukes seemed a reasonable response. They just had a much more pronounced effect on the bodhisattvas and their spirit minions than on Ravnos - who was either not very bothered by them or actually just completely unaffected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:35:53-07:00","id":857292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=857153#post857153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never saw stats for Lesser Uktena in the tribebook or Axis Mundi. Maybe you are referencing the lackluster stats in that one Mind's Eye book? I don't like going to other systems for statistics and see those as apocryphal guidelines at best. I figured it was implied to be a 'win button' power that then requires your character to slither off into Uktena's tribal homeland after you get your crowning moment of awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's all in the Revised Tribebook. Not very super effective, compared to Leviathan adding 5 to all of your Chasmus physical attributes and giving you automatic Rage regen with absolutely no downsides..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:11:25-07:00","id":857399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=857153#post857153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to be totally off-base regarding the Week of Nightmares... huffing glue is worse than I thought. Oops.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I never saw stats for Lesser Uktena in the tribebook or Axis Mundi. Maybe you are referencing the lackluster stats in that one Mind's Eye book? I don't like going to other systems for statistics and see those as apocryphal guidelines at best. I figured it was implied to be a 'win button' power that then requires your character to slither off into Uktena's tribal homeland after you get your crowning moment of awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well yeah, if you give Paws to Garou who are not rank 5, I imagine it will be easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 4+ , that includes 5 and 6. It also includes the gifts spirit of the fray, command spirit , call of Gaia, reshape spirit, a bunch of X 2 Dmg gifts and other stuff. Rank 3+ gifts are pretty bad ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:29:39-07:00","id":857535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855503-it-seems-that-vampires-and-kuei-jin-get-beaten-by-a-lot-of-the-other-splats?p=857399#post857399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arro